# Coffee Cake

Based on [https://www.compasscoffee.com/…](https://www.compasscoffee.com/blogs/the-daily-grind/coffee-cake) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251008102110/https://www.compasscoffee.com/blogs/the-daily-grind/coffee-cake))

{ rating="5" image="coffee_cake.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### For the Cake:

- [ ] 2 cups [all-purpose flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }
- [ ] 1 cup [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }
- [ ] 1 cup [milk]{ ing="milk" }
- [ ] 2 large [eggs]{ ing="egg" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [baking powder]{ ing="baking-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [vanilla extract]{ ing="vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] A pinch of [salt]{ ing="salt" }

### For the Cinnamon Topping:

- [ ] 1/2 cup [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [ground cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup [melted butter]{ ing="melted-butter" }

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350F (175C)
1. Grease a 9x13-inch baking dish with [butter]{ ing="melted-butter" }
1. Mix the dry ingredients in a large mixing bowl and the wet ingredients in a medium one. Combine and mix until smooth; keep the medium bowl. Pour into the baking dish
1. In the medium mixing bowl, combine the [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" } and [cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" } for the topping. Drizzle the [melted butter]{ ing="melted-butter" } into the mix and stir until it looks like sand

   1. Spoon the [cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" } mixture over the batter and use a knife to swirl it in
1. Bake for 25-35 minutes or until a toothpick comes out clean

## Notes

- *Good, but I would like to try a recipe that adds a crumble top*
